%PDF-2.0
%‚„œ”
% CalibratedColorTest.pdf - graphical tests for the CIE-based color spaces CalGray, CalRGB and Lab.
%
% Rules
% - One page per feature. Each row is one case: one color space, optionally under a graphics state
%   (UseBlackPtComp) or a rendering intent (ri). Each column is one input value, the same for every
%   row of a page, so a feature's effect reads down a column.
% - Only valid input: WhitePoint Y = 1, BlackPoint non-negative and not above WhitePoint.
% - BlackPoint cases are written as k x WhitePoint, so they stay neutral relative to the white.
% - Every page ends with a control row in a device space, for checking the capture itself.
% - Pages are 1100 x 940. Grid: 12 columns x 12 rows, pitch 70, tiles 60 x 60 with 10 gutters.
%   Tile (column c, row r), row 0 at the top: left = 230 + 70c, top = 870 - 70r.
%   Unused rows stay empty. Black 8 x 8 registration squares mark the four outer corners of the full
%   12 x 12 grid, centers (212, 888), (1078, 888), (212, 22), (1078, 22). They are the only small
%   pure black objects on a page: all text is 0.4 gray, so a measuring script can find them.
%   Each used tile has a light gray 0.5 outline 1.5 outside it, in the gutter, so white tiles show.
% - Row labels are left of the grid, column inputs above it; no text inside the grid.
% - Columns:
%   CalRGB pages: gray ramp 0 .02 .05 .10 .20 .35 .50 .75 1, then R, G, B at full.
%   CalGray page: 0 .02 .05 .10 .15 .20 .35 .50 .65 .75 .90 1.
%   Lab pages: L* 0 5 20 50 75 100 at a* = b* = 0, then L* 60 at chroma 30 every 60 degrees of hue:
%   (60 30 0) (60 15 26) (60 -15 26) (60 -30 0) (60 -15 -26) (60 15 -26). These stay inside sRGB for
%   every WhitePoint used, adapted with Bradford or by XYZ scaling.
%   Lab control row: DeviceRGB holding the exact sRGB of each column read as D50 Lab (8.6.5.4).
% - Image rows are 12 x 1, 8-bit images with the default Decode for their space; inputs are rounded
%   to the nearest code value.
% - Matrices are named after the working space they resemble; values are the common published ones.
% - Pages:
%   1. CalRGB baseline: common working spaces, no BlackPoint
%   2. CalRGB WhitePoint: sRGB-like matrix, G 2.2, WhitePoint varies
%   3. CalRGB Gamma: sRGB-like matrix, D65, Gamma varies
%   4. CalRGB Matrix: D65, G 2.2, Matrix varies
%   5. CalRGB BlackPoint, realistic: sRGB-like, BlackPoint = k x WhitePoint
%   6. CalRGB BlackPoint, upper range and tinted: sRGB-like
%   7. CalRGB BlackPoint against UseBlackPtComp and rendering intent: sRGB-like
%   8. CalGray: Gamma, WhitePoint, BlackPoint = k x WhitePoint
%   9. Lab baseline: fills and 8-bit images
%   10. Lab WhitePoint: Range omitted, WhitePoint varies
%   11. Lab Range: D50, Range varies
%   12. Lab BlackPoint, realistic: BlackPoint = k x WhitePoint
%   13. Lab BlackPoint, upper range and tinted
%   14. Lab against UseBlackPtComp and rendering intent
% - Edit by hand. The xref is a stub with a bogus startxref: readers repair it by scanning the objects,
%   so no offsets need maintaining. Keep /Root in the trailer pointing at the catalog, and keep each
%   stream's /Length right.
